  "lore": {
    "energy": "A central power core charges a 1.2 GJ optical-energy budget between passes. Rotating containment cages circulate the fictional storage fields; charging losses and waste heat are additional.",
    "thermal": "Embedded radiator sectors reject heat during recovery. Sustained phase alignment depletes field stability, so the cages must return to their charging paths after at most ten seconds.",
    "optics": "Three nested cages converge to maintain a clear polar corridor. A stabilized lens train sustains the continuous 1.064 µm beam for the ten-second energy window. The engine drives OPTICS_YAW and OPTICS_PITCH; beam effects remain external.",
    "name": "SOL-88 is the standalone Syzygy orbital-laser model, separate from the original SOL-82 satellite."
  },
